# Keep the embedded onboarding fixtures byte-identical across platforms. Without this,
# git normalizes the CSV to LF in the repo while Windows checks out CRLF, so the Linux
# (Railway Docker) build embedded LF-only bytes — which parsed to an EMPTY order on prod
# while Windows dev (CRLF) parsed fine. Force CRLF so every build embeds the same bytes.
ProcuLink.Api/Fixtures/*.csv text eol=crlf
ProcuLink.Infrastructure/Fixtures/*.csv text eol=crlf

# Vendored OASIS UBL 2.1 schemas — byte-for-byte, no EOL translation, for two reasons.
#   LICENCE: the OASIS notice grants redistribution only of the UNMODIFIED document.
#            Rewriting every line ending is a modification, so `-text` is a compliance
#            requirement here and not a preference.
#   CORRECTNESS: core.autocrlf is true on Windows dev machines and absent in the Linux CI
#            container, so without this the embedded resource bytes — and therefore the
#            SHA-256 digests pinned in PROVENANCE.md — would differ by platform. Exactly
#            the split the CSV rule above exists to close.
ProcuLink.Transform/Conformance/Schemas/ubl-2.1/**/*.xsd -text
